{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789290373,"nonce":"sZRIyQjYenFix/x9Zgfh2ILXjrE=","title":"Let a host add roots to the reachability sweep","message":"reachable::analyze seeds from the entrypoint and treats direct calls and\nclosure findexes as exact. Three consumers skip what it calls dead: the\nAIR pipeline's passes (air_pipeline.rs ~1637, ~1687, ~1727) and the AOT\nshard sweep (aot_shard.rs sweep_unreachable), which deletes about a third\nof a module. Under a host, other languages call into Haxe classes the\nHaxe program itself never references, so from the entrypoint they are\ndead: their AIR is never optimised, and an AOT build emits no body for\nthem, so a linked spoke has no symbol to bind. Static linking cannot\nhelp; it preserves what was emitted.\n\nAdd a seam entry: `reach_roots() -\u003e the set of findexes a host has\npublished`, filled by the host through hlp_rt_install alongside the\nheap and scheduler slots (or a separate `hlp_reach_add_root(findex)`),\nconsulted by reachable::analyze as extra seeds. Default empty, so ash\nalone is unchanged. The interpreter needs nothing: it keeps every\nfunction and the whole type table.\n\nRelated: the Haxe compiler's own DCE is a separate layer, handled on the\ncaribou side with @:keep from a build macro.","files":null}]}